---
/**
 * communities-shutdown.astro — X Communities 关停专题页
 *
 * Fact-checked 2026-11-12 against Nikita Bier's posts, TechCrunch, Engadget,
 * and The Verge. The May 30, 2026 date is an announced transition deadline.
 * X has not posted a later confirmation that Communities were removed.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {
  XCHAT_CHAT_URL,
  XCHAT_TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_URL,
} from '../data/xchat';

const DATE_MODIFIED = '2026-11-12';
const DEADLINE_ISO = '2026-05-30T00:00:00Z';
const DEADLINE_DISPLAY = 'May 30, 2026';
const deadlinePassed = Date.now() >= new Date(DEADLINE_ISO).getTime();

const articleJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: `X Communities shutdown was announced for ${DEADLINE_DISPLAY}`,
  description:
    'X head of product Nikita Bier said in April 2026 that Communities would be deprecated, with a transition deadline of May 30, 2026. Removal has not been confirmed in a later X, TechCrunch, or Verge report.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'XChat Hub' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'XChat Hub', url: 'https://xchat.directory' },
  datePublished: '2026-04-24',
  dateModified: DATE_MODIFIED,
};

const migrationSteps = [
  {
    step: 1,
    title: 'Open chat in the X app',
    desc: `Chat launched inside X on iOS and the web in November 2025, with Android described as coming soon (<a href="https://www.theverge.com/news/821950/x-chat-encrypted-dms-video-calls" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Verge</a>). A separate iOS app followed on April 24, 2026 (<a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/24/x-launches-xchat-app-ios-messaging-iphone/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a>). You can also try <a href="${XCHAT_CHAT_URL}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">chat.x.com</a> and sign in with your X account.`,
  },
  {
    step: 2,
    title: 'Create a group and a public link',
    desc: 'On April 22, 2026, Nikita Bier said XChat group chats supported joinable public links, with 350 members per chat “and growing.” The next day he said the limit would rise to 500 and that X would aim for 1,000. Those higher caps were a plan, not a later confirmation.',
  },
  {
    step: 3,
    title: 'Pin the link where members will see it',
    desc: 'Bier told Community admins to pin the group-chat link so members could join during the transition window. Post it on your timeline as well. A QR code is not described in those posts.',
  },
  {
    step: 4,
    title: 'Tell people this is a chat, not a feed',
    desc: 'Engadget noted that a live group chat is a different product from a Community’s separate timeline. Bier also pointed to Custom Timelines for topic feeds. Check in the app whether new members need approval; the April posts do not spell that step out.',
  },
];

const features = [
  {
    icon: '🔒',
    title: 'Encryption X has described',
    desc: 'X says chats and file sharing are end-to-end encrypted. The Verge, citing X’s support page, reports that metadata is not covered and that users would not know if X itself compromised a conversation. “Encrypted by default” for every chat is not confirmed.',
  },
  {
    icon: '🔗',
    title: 'Joinable group links',
    desc: 'Bier said admins can create a public group-chat link and share it on the timeline. That is the migration path he described.',
  },
  {
    icon: '📱',
    title: 'Inside X, plus the web',
    desc: 'The Verge reported Chat on iOS and the web in November 2025. TechCrunch reported a standalone iOS app on April 24, 2026. It was not an iPhone-only product from the first day.',
  },
  {
    icon: '👥',
    title: 'Group size X stated',
    desc: '350 members “and growing” on April 22. A plan for 500 the next day, and a goal of 1,000 within a couple of weeks. TechCrunch reported the 500 figure and the 1,000 goal. A shipped 1,000 cap is not confirmed.',
  },
  {
    icon: '💬',
    title: 'A chat, not a ranked feed',
    desc: 'Engadget contrasted group chat with Communities’ asynchronous feed. X has not said XChat has no ranking, no suggestions, or no shadowbanning.',
  },
  {
    icon: '🎙️',
    title: 'Calls, not voice channels',
    desc: 'The Verge and TechCrunch report voice and video calls. TechCrunch also reported voice notes in April 2026. Persistent “voice channels” are not described in those reports.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="X Communities Shutting Down 2026 — What X Announced"
  description="X said in April 2026 that Communities would be deprecated, with a May 30 transition deadline. Removal is not confirmed. What was sourced about XChat group links."
  jsonLd={articleJsonLd}
  canonicalPath="/communities-shutdown"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://xchat.directory/' },
    { name: 'X Communities Alternative', url: 'https://xchat.directory/communities-shutdown/' },
  ]}
>
  <!-- ==================== HERO ==================== -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">{deadlinePassed ? 'Deadline passed · removal not confirmed' : 'Shutdown announced'}</span>
      <h1>
        X Communities shutdown<br />
        <span class="text-gradient">announced for {DEADLINE_DISPLAY}.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead text-secondary prose-body">
        On April 22, 2026, X head of product Nikita Bier
        <a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047041338106159484" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">said X was deprecating Communities on May 6</a>
        and told admins to pin a joinable XChat group link.
        The next day he
        <a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047147126183137468" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">moved that transition window to <time datetime="2026-05-30">{DEADLINE_DISPLAY}</time></a>.
        <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/23/x-is-shutting-down-communities-because-of-low-usage-and-lots-of-spam/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a>
        and
        <a href="https://www.engadget.com/social-media/x-is-shutting-down-its-communities-feature-182843958.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Engadget</a>
        reported the plan. X has not posted a later confirmation that the feature was removed.
      </p>
      <p class="text-secondary" style="font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: -0.5rem;">
        Last updated <time datetime={DATE_MODIFIED}>November 12, 2026</time>.
      </p>

      <div class="countdown-strip" aria-label="Announced X Communities transition deadline">
        <div class="count-box">
          <span class="count-num">{DEADLINE_DISPLAY}</span>
          <span class="count-label">{deadlinePassed ? 'Announced deadline has passed' : 'Announced transition deadline'}</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href={XCHAT_CHAT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          Open chat.x.com
        </a>
        <a href="/how-to-create-group-link" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">
          How to Create Group Link
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== WHY MIGRATE ==================== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="col-text">
          <h2>What X said would replace Communities</h2>
          <p class="text-secondary prose-body">
            Twitter launched Communities in 2021, according to
            <a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/23/x-is-shutting-down-communities-because-of-low-usage-and-lots-of-spam/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch</a>.
            Bier’s reason for deprecating them, in a
            <a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047180747690434994" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reply on April 23</a>,
            was that they “were used by less than 0.4% of users—yet contributed to 80% of spam reports, financial scams, and malware on X.”
            Those figures are his, not an independent audit.
          </p>
          <p class="text-secondary prose-body">
            He told admins to move members into XChat group chats, and he also said X was investing in niche communities through Custom Timelines.
            Engadget described XChat as the proposed chat replacement and Custom Timelines as the path for a topic feed.
            Calling XChat the only official replacement overstates that.
          </p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Joinable group links, which Bier told admins to pin</li>
            <li>X says chats can be end-to-end encrypted; default encryption for every chat is not confirmed</li>
            <li>Voice and video calls, as The Verge reported — not voice channels</li>
            <li>Screenshot blocking is an option X has described, not a setting confirmed as on by default</li>
            <li>Same X account, because Chat is X’s own messaging</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-visual">
          <div class="comparison-card">
            <h3>X Communities</h3>
            <ul class="bad-list">
              <li>Separate feed of posts, launched 2021</li>
              <li>Bier: under 0.4% of users, heavy spam reports</li>
              <li>Deprecation announced for May 6, then May 30</li>
              <li>Removal after that date: not confirmed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="comparison-card good">
            <h3>XChat group chats</h3>
            <ul class="good-list">
              <li>Public join links, per Bier’s April 22 post</li>
              <li>X says messages and files can be E2EE, with limits The Verge reported</li>
              <li>Voice and video calls reported; voice channels not described</li>
              <li>350 members stated; 500 and 1,000 were the next targets</li>
              <li>Chat in the X app since November 2025; iOS app April 24, 2026</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== FEATURE GRID ==================== -->
  <section class="section features-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">What You Get with XChat</h2>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        {features.map((f) => (
          <article class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{f.icon}</span>
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-secondary">{f.desc}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== MIGRATION STEPS ==================== -->
  <section class="section steps-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Migrate in 4 Steps</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        {migrationSteps.map((s) => (
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-number">{s.step}</div>
            <div class="step-content">
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-secondary" set:html={s.desc} />
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== SOURCES ==================== -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Sources checked November 12, 2026</h2>
      <ul class="checklist source-list">
        <li><a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047041338106159484" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nikita Bier, April 22, 2026</a> — deprecating Communities on May 6; joinable group links; 350 members and growing; Custom Timelines.</li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047147126183137468" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nikita Bier, April 23, 2026</a> — transition window through May 30; plan to raise the cap to 500, aiming for 1,000.</li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/nikitabier/status/2047180747690434994" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nikita Bier, April 23, 2026</a> — under 0.4% of users; 80% of spam reports, financial scams, and malware.</li>
        <li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/23/x-is-shutting-down-communities-because-of-low-usage-and-lots-of-spam/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch, April 23, 2026</a> — reported the shutdown plan, the May 30 extension, and the 500 / 1,000 group-size targets.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/social-media/x-is-shutting-down-its-communities-feature-182843958.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Engadget, April 23, 2026</a> — reported the same announcement and the difference between a chat and a Community feed.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/news/821950/x-chat-encrypted-dms-video-calls" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Verge, November 17, 2025</a> — X says Chat supports E2EE for messages and files; metadata and insider compromise are not covered; screenshot notify-or-block is an option; voice and video calls.</li>
        <li><a href="https://x.com/chat/status/1989465741444485180" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@chat, November 14, 2025</a> — X’s own claim of encrypted chats, disappearing messages, and screenshot blocking or notifications.</li>
        <li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/24/x-launches-xchat-app-ios-messaging-iphone/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch, April 24, 2026</a> — standalone iOS app; X claims encryption and screenshot blocking; experts have disputed the encryption claim.</li>
        <li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/09/x-brings-back-voice-notes-to-x-chat/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TechCrunch, April 9, 2026</a> — voice notes in one-to-one and group chats; calls and screenshot options also described.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== FINAL CTA ==================== -->
  <section class="section final-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="final-card">
        <h2>If you still need to move members</h2>
        <p class="text-secondary prose-body">
          Bier’s advice to admins was to pin an XChat group link before the May 30 deadline he set.
          Whether a given Community still opens is not something X, TechCrunch, or The Verge confirmed after that date.
          Check the app, then use the group link if you want the path X described.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-buttons" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <a href={XCHAT_CHAT_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Open chat.x.com
          </a>
          <a href={XCHAT_TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">
            Get Migration Tips on Telegram
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ---- Hero ---- */
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: 4rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-light);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding: 0.3125rem 0.875rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.05);
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto 1.25rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* ---- Countdown Strip ---- */
  .countdown-strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
  }

  .count-box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 99, 71, 0.35);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 99, 71, 0.08), rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.04));
  }

  .count-num {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: #ff6347;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .source-list li {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .source-list a {
    color: var(--accent-light);
  }

  .count-label {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-top: 0.375rem;
  }

  /* ---- Two Column ---- */
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .col-text h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .checklist li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ---- Comparison Cards ---- */
  .col-visual {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .comparison-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .comparison-card.good {
    border-color: rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.3);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.08), transparent);
  }

  .comparison-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .comparison-card.good h3 {
    color: var(--accent-light);
  }

  .bad-list, .good-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .bad-list li, .good-list li {
    padding: 0.375rem 0;
  }

  /* ---- Features ---- */
  .features-section {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.03), transparent);
  }

  .section-title {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    transition: border-color 0.2s, transform 0.2s;
  }

  .feature-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-hover);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .feature-icon {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ---- Steps ---- */
  .steps-section {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .steps {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .step-number {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .step-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .step-content p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ---- Final CTA ---- */
  .final-section {
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .final-card {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at top, rgba(29, 155, 240, 0.08), transparent 60%),
      var(--bg-card);
  }

  .final-card h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  /* ---- Responsive ---- */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .two-col {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .col-visual {
      order: -1;
    }
    .feature-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
